instruction:
 Use structured text (ST) to design a PLC function block named 'CALCULATE_OUTPUT'.
The function block receives an integer input 'i' and produces an output 'o' based on the value of 'i'.
The output is determined as follows: when the input 'i' is 0, the output 'o' is 0;
when the input is between 1 and 5, 'o' is the square of 'i';
when 'i' is between 6 and 10, 'o' is equal to 'i' plus two times 'i';
otherwise, 'o' is assigned a value of -1.
The program should ensure valid bounds for 'i' and that 'o' never takes undefined or invalid values.

FUNCTION_BLOCK FB_CalculateOutput
VAR_INPUT
i: INT;
END_VAR
VAR_OUTPUT
o: INT;
END_VAR

END_FUNCTION_BLOCK
